---
// INTERNAL PREVIEW CHROME — full nav on the review site, gate untouched on the
// live domains.
//
// The soft-launch gate (public/_redirects + src/data/launch-gate.ts) leaves two
// pages open to the public — / and /ag/hogs-livestock/ — and both render the
// Header/Footer in `minimal` mode so no nav link leads into a gated page. That
// also strips the nav on securelogic.netlify.app, which is NOT gated and is the
// URL the team reviews the site on, so those two pages became dead ends for
// internal review.
//
// One build serves both hosts, so the choice has to be made in the browser.
// This component parks a second, full-nav copy of the chrome in an inert
// <template>: nothing inside it is rendered, matched by document.querySelector,
// initialised by Alpine, or fetched (images included). The swap script at the
// bottom of BaseLayout replaces `replaces` with the copy, but only on localhost
// and *.netlify.app. Because template contents sit outside the document tree,
// the selector cannot accidentally match the copy itself.
//
// Fail-closed on purpose: the live domains get the minimal chrome by rendering
// it, not by suppressing anything, so a blocked or broken script leaves
// genesis360.com exactly as it is today. Delete this component (and the two
// usages) when SOFT_LAUNCH goes false — the real chrome is full by default.
interface Props {
  // CSS selector for the live minimal element this copy stands in for. Both
  // roots are unique per page: Header renders a single `.sh` wrapper, Footer a
  // single `<footer class="bl ...">`. A sibling position would be simpler but
  // is not safe here — Astro inlines Header's bundled script directly after the
  // header, so previousElementSibling lands on a <script>.
  replaces: string;
}

const { replaces } = Astro.props;
---

<template data-preview-chrome={replaces}><slot /></template>
